on  problems we see that the auc  is higher and for the regression  problems the msc  is very slightly here's almost exactly  the same  and here is slightly better using snap  ml  okay next chart please  okay so um in this chart we we  compare against a different framework um  so we  also switch gears a bit uh in the  previous three benchmarks we were  looking at the cpu  performance and now we're looking at the  gpu performance  and we're comparing here to the qml  framework from nvidia which is a  software for accelerated classical  machine learning  on gpus so on the left hand side we  compare for  uh ridge regression uh which is like a  l2 regularized linear regression  and on the right for logistic first for  classification problems  and the y-axis here shows the speed up  we achieved  over um qml so we see  in some cases um qml was ever so  slightly better  and in other cases snappermill was 164  times better  68 times better on logistic and this  these speed ups are coming from the fact  that we solve the problem  using fundamentally different algorithms  than cool ml  and this is this is um related to the  core research  technology which is underpinning the  snuff and wealth framework  okay next chart please  okay so now i'd like to talk a bit about  the  accuracy games that one can achieve  using  uh snappermill and in particular using a  snapboost  or boosting machine so  um this is one of the first benchmarks  we did with  snapboost in the beginning um using the  openml platform so openml is like a  platform for collaborative data science  it has it hosts  thousands of data sets um which you can  easily download download using  which makes it uh well suited for doing  these kind of benchmarks where you  it's very it's very important to compare  different boosting machines using a  large number of data sets  because uh with a single data set it's  hard to  say um which one is really better you  need a large sample  enable to be able to make um conclusive  